Z||000000||theogre||09-16-2001||01:50 AM||||Ogre has had enough. I'm sure I'm about to piss some people off. My only hope is Maybe I'll make a few people think.<P>I've been asked why I don't respond to the various WTC related threads. Frankly way too many people are posting out of anger and ignorance. Being pissed is a normal part of grieving. Being absurd and stupid isn't.<P>The big reason is I don't think most people understand even the most basic concepts of what a Jihad is. Study the Crusades sometime. The Crusades where the Catholic version of Jihad. Fat lot of good it did them. They got the crap kicked out of them.<P>The people behind this will fight to the last man woman and child. For every terrorist we arrest/kill there are a dozen other wating to take their place.<P>You aren't dealing with a country. You are trying to kill an idea. Ideas don't die easy, especially when the idea is supported by people who believe they are glorified by dieing for it. How many Christians got fed to lions over their idea that Christ died for them?<P>1. Would people please get their facts straight before posting things reguarding the WTC attack. Incorrect information serves no-one but the people behind this and the scam spam running all over the place.<P>2. Do some basic reserch on the current Afghanistan/Bin Laden situation. The U.S. trained many of these people durring the USSR occupation of Afghanistan years ago. The CIA, etc, was more than happy to dump resources into Bin Ladan and others when it suited them. All the time many of them wondered if it would come back to bite them in the ass. They simply didn't give a sh_t becaue it was the USSR that was the Evil Empire of the day. (This was even covered on tonites Americas Most Wanted 2 hour event.)<P>3. Don't blame all Arabs or Muslims for this. This is the work of fundimentalist/raceist/purist factions and not the general population. Many of the Afghanis aren't any more happy about living under Taliban rule than anyone else. They had a nice happy blend of western and other styles going in their lives. The Taliban has trashed most of it. On the other hand the Taliban has done something no other government, including the U.S. DEA, has managed... they have killed one of the largest opium productions in the world. (If you want an interesting take on drugs... read the Bio of a Space Tyrant books. Written by Piers Anthony of Xanth fame as I remember... )<P>Has WWIII begun? I would not be at all suprised. NATO has signed on under Article 5 of the treaty. That means around 18 counties pluss non NATO Russia have agreed to work on this. Even China appears in on this one and they never want in on anything outside their borders.<P>Someone asked about a Draft... Could be entirely posible. As they say, The Sh_t has hit the fan. Only God knows where it will go now.<P>Have we seen the last major casualty list on a civilian target? I doubt it. There are plenty of ways around the FAA's "increased security" rules and plenty of other targets you don't need aircraft for. Has everyone already forgotten the Sarin attack in Japan's subways a couple years ago? Chemical weapons aren't hard to come by. Wakeup and suck air thru your gas mask....<P>Is it just me? Has no-one considered that a war is exactly what these people want. They know there is no fixed target. You can't just drop a few smart bombs on them. That's been tried. Only made them move camp. Short of Genocide there is no way to stop them. Hitler tried that solution against the Jews in the 40's and I would hope everyone knows how far that got...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||4
Z||000001||Mach10||09-16-2001||02:06 AM||||Harsh, but to the point. A lot of people would do well to put aside their hate and listen.<BR><P>------------------<BR>"Duct Tape is Good to Mach 3"<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.escape.ca/~fogg/halfpole.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||maryjane||09-16-2001||02:08 AM||||Nope it's not just you, I've been hammerin away tryin to tell everyone this is going to be a long, dirty, ugly mess. With lots of casualties.Killin the wrong or innocent people are going to be the least of our problems before this is played out. Not very<BR>many options tho, unless you advocate 'turning the other cheek' and write off the thousands already dead. Better enjoy the upcoming holidays, may not be much to celebrate next year. Hope I'm wrong. Care to offer an alternative, Ogre?<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 09-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Leper||09-16-2001||02:21 AM||||I do too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||09-16-2001||08:12 AM||||I hope this doesn't come to all out war.  Even though the "free world" would be the victors, I don't think there would really  be a "winner".  Everyone would lose.  On the other hand, I would be very angry and very disappointed if we simply turned the other cheek.  We need to eliminate bin Laden from...  I don't necessarily mean killing him, either.  (That's what I'd probably do if I met him face to face, though.)  If we kill him, he becomes a martyr.  Somehow, I don't think that prison is enough, either.  <P>I don't want war, but I do want whatever it takes to keep this from ever happening again.  If it means flattening a few Mid East countries, so be it.  If it's possible to end this with just the apprehension of a few select individuals, then that would be the better choice although I really don't see that as an end to this madness.  As far as ways to get around the increased security measures, it's already been done by some pilots the other day.  They just wanted to see if it was possible.  (You couldn't pay me to get on an airplane at this point.)  <P>What's the solution?  Who knows.  Obviously the US gov't doesn't or something would have been implemented by now.  This is a tough call.  If this was just the work of one or two demented madmen (i.e. lunatics like Hitler or Stalin, etc) then the solution would be easy.  Eliminate them by any means, fair or foul.  This may be different.  Will the elimination of bin Laden (and possibly others such as Saddam) solve the problem?  I doubt terrorism will go away as there are plenty of others who would love to fill their shoes.  But...it might slow things down enough to make time to find a solution.  We are under the gun (so to speak) to find a quick end to this right now.  If we don't do anything, will we have another bloodbath next week?  Maybe the week after?<P>Ogre is right when he says not to blame all Arabs or Muslims for this.  My wifes' motel was recently bought out by Indians (not Native Americans).  While I don't think very highly of them or their work ethics, they seem to be very much against what is happening.  They aren't American citizens yet they're still doing what they can to show support for the US.  (They're Hindu, if that makes any difference.)  <P>Ogre makes a good point regarding other, non airline related targets.  I'm not as worried about NBC weapons as I am about the E bomb.  (What?  Nobody's heard of that one?  Wouldn't hurt a 3<sup>rd</sup> world country nearly as bad as it would hurt us.)  Those don't necessarily have to be detonated in the air.  These can be disguised as radios, TV parts, etc.  And any country can make them.  I though about this when the WTC/Pentagon debacle 1<sup>st</sup> happened, but thought that if I mentioned it, it would give the terrorists a new idea.  I realize that was stupid as they've though of everything I could possibly think of already.<P>I'm out of shape, overweight and have very few military skills, but if I thought that the military could use my services and it would make a difference, I'd try to enlist in a minute.  <P>I'm still trying to understand why some of the Mid Easterners living in the US would cheer when this happened.  If they hate the US so much, why are they here?  As I've said before, maybe they were just caught up in the moment.  This doesn't mean that I think they were right in cheering, but maybe they've had time to think thing over and come to the conclusion that this really isn't such a good thing.  If they love Osama bin Laden so much, they would be "over there" instead of living the good life here.<P>I believe I've rambled on long enough.  Just my take on a few things.<BR><P>------------------<BR>In memory of those that died on 11 Sept 2001.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1367.gif">  <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||1
