Z||000006||theogre||09-16-2001||12:31 PM||||I have no alternative for anything to do with this right now. I'm just hoping they don't rush in to things halfassed. It's way to easy right now for someone with a itchy finger to start all hell breaking loose and make things far worse than they already are.<P>One other thought.... Don't take press reports as gosple right now. Major mistakes are being made. There have already been multiple retractions of stories. The bigest example is two guys they said were on the plains as hijackers... One is alive and well and working with FBI, and the other died in a small plane crash a year ago. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||09-16-2001||01:47 PM||||The worst thing Bush could do(and I doubt he will) is start this thing half-assed. I watch the news about this, but know at least 50% of it is trash.<P>IMO Ogre, you are blowing this out of proportion(friendly disagreement, I can't beat you with infomation and facts). Osama/Afghanistan don't appear to have much going for them. Even their neighbors are siding with the U.S. and others. I don't see a draft starting(so many nations are willing to go at it), and I don't think it will classify as a WW without a major surprise. My fear is having an allie(s) switch sides as this fires up. That would almost certainly classify as WW.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Loki||09-16-2001||02:09 PM||||Well spoken Ogre... Either way we go its a no win situation in my eyes. <P>1) We attack, they fight back causing more damage and loss of life.<BR>2) We dont attack, they basically just beat America. And they keep on with the loss of life.<BR>No one country is to blame, its the way certain people are. Like with American's being racist.  Its a sad day for all American's but we have to find the right way to handle this and not drag it out, or there WILL be a great loss of life.  <P>Remember this is in my eyes and the way I see things. The terrorist's did what they set out to do and succeded greatly.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">  <BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000009||Tonker||09-16-2001||04:27 PM||||Well put. <P>There is no easy solution. I think there are wrong solutions that are a lot easier, but I will continue to disagree the people who suggest them. I think we can overcome this problem in the long run, though. In the meantime it's going to be a long, hard struggle.<p>[This message has been edited by Tonker (edited 09-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||btoth||09-16-2001||05:15 PM||||I wish that the media would just shut up and stop with the b/s info and all the "analyst" crap and the "what ifs".  Every person with a brain can come up with their own "what ifs", we don't need people coming up with them for us.  The news should go back to their regular news at 5 and 11 (or whatever) and report the FACTS and ONLY the facts and only have "special reports" when the Pres. or some other high-ranking government official with something important to say is holding a press conference.  <P>I don't know everything there is to know about our politics with the Middle East.  And no matter how much I like to think I'm not gullible or a follower of the crowd, I fall for the rumors and the b/s and make judgments without knowing the facts, and I know I'm not the only one.<P>Anyway, this is all just a bunch of rambling.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  But I would like to mention something about a concert I went to last night... Tool, at the CSU Convocation Center:<P>During a break in the music, Maynard (the lead singer) was saying something about it being "an emotional week" and "a time for healing". (I was pretty much deaf at the time.)  The crowed had some remarks (most stupid and rude remarks of course from a bunch of drunk people), and then started chanting "USA, USA, USA".  After the crowed died down, Maynard quietly replied with "this is not a political forum, but a time for healing" and something about "worldly consciousness" followed by "not fueling ignorance".  Way to go Maynard.<P>OK, I'm done.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Wolfhound||09-16-2001||05:22 PM||||Theogre, Interesting note: You mention a highjackers name being someone killed in a plane crash a year ago.<BR> <BR>This was the brother of one of the actual highjackers who was killed in a midair collision in Vero Beach. Ameer Bukhari, brother of actual highjacker Adnan Bukahri.<P>He also was going through the same flight training and lived in Vero with his brother.<P>I found this in a on line newspaper article from Vero Beach. I have friends in Vero that live less than a mile from the house they rented.<P>Did Ameer get in too much practice or was he setting an example. Scarry thought!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 09-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||MontanaFiero||09-17-2001||04:32 AM||||I personally agree with the Ogre mostly. I am very worried that there may be hundreds more "radicals" living throughout the United States just waiting for the word "go". Then we will all be sorry.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <P><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>I pray that the Lord, Jesus Christ, who <I>is</I> Our Savior, takes the reins from this point on to guide us into a resolution that will prevent more pain and suffering. God Bless us all.</B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000013||theogre||09-17-2001||07:49 PM||||This kind of crap is why we have the Second Amendment... Who's going to get there faster?<P>A. Call 911 and wade thru their bs, then wait while some moron prioritizes the call. Finally, after at least several minutes, if you are lucky, an officer will be dispatched. Then it will take however long to cover the distance between where he is and you are.<P>B. The "red neck" with a shot gun or rifle in his vehicle.<P>C. The Law Abiding conceled carry guy with a gun in his belt.<P>Well... C is out... large numbers of places ban concealed carry. That's when handguns or all guns aren't banned as they are in NYC.<P>B. Is out in allot of places to. The gun in the truck/trunk is only common in more rural areas like most of upstate NY.<P>That leaves you with A... With the rare exception, Best case is the cop gets there in no less than 10-20 minutes. This is NOT the cop's fault. They simply can't be everywhere. Terrorists know that. So do most speeders and redlight runners.<P>Allot of people pushing gun control regularly claimed no-one would ever lodge a serious attack on U.S. Soil. Boy were they wrong. <P>I hate to scare people but I have little doubt those airplanes where the end of what's comming. There are far more other things to go after and many of them are potentially more damaging than WTC. You might not get the body count of WTC but you can make sure no-one will live in that area for a long time.<P>Would a gun have stopped Tuesdays attack? Likely not. It might stop the next jackass that tries something.<P>Those of you that do plan to fly... keep your seat belt on at all times unless you have to use the restroom or something. Pilots and their reps have already said they will do whatever they have to in future "and they [the attackers] won't be walking afterward."||||reg||1
